<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net">
  <diagram name="Results" id="results1">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1500" pageHeight="2080" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />

        <mxCell id="title" value="Real-Data Backtest Results: REAL Dispatch vs. TRAINED Model (Cycle-Based)" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=20;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontColor=#1A1A1A;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="20" width="1380" height="34" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="subtitle" value="1,667 real historical orders, 42 real drivers -- TRAINED's candidate pool limited to the SAME 42 drivers REAL used. A CYCLE = one full loop, home base to home base -- see glossary below." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=12;fontStyle=2;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontColor=#666666;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="58" width="1380" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ===== Glossary ===== -->
        <mxCell id="gloss_hdr" value="How to Read These Results: What a &quot;Cycle&quot; Is" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5F5F5;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="100" width="1380" height="35" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gloss_body" value="&#8226; CYCLE: one full loop for a driver -- leaving home base, working a sequence of real trips, and returning to home base. Every cycle is closed one of two ways; there is no &quot;incomplete, excluded&quot; case.&#xa;&#8226; Closed by a real paid trip: a real order's own destination happens to BE the driver's home hub -- 0 empty miles, the trip itself completed the return.&#xa;&#8226; Closed by a real SIMULATED deadhead leg (TRAINED only): the simulator's own post-delivery repositioning mechanic puts the driver at the home hub while more of the data window remains -- a real, priced empty distance, not a guess.&#xa;&#8226; Closed by an ASSUMED empty return (&quot;no trip&quot;): the driver is not observed back at home base by the time the data runs out -- that remaining gap to home IS the empty-return-miles metric, priced at real routed distance. REAL can ONLY ever close a cycle this way or via a real paid trip -- it has no record of an empty-only leg at all, so an assumed return is REAL's only way to represent &quot;didn't find a load home.&quot;&#xa;&#8226; HOS remaining at return: legal driving/duty hours still available but UNUSED once back home -- real forgone capacity. Reconstructed for REAL from the SAME seeded starting HOS condition TRAINED's own simulated fleet uses (identical random seed), walked forward through REAL's own actual pickup/delivery timestamps -- a real reconstruction, not an assumption about REAL.&#xa;&#8226; All 42 of these real drivers show home hub = London in the source data (none = Milton) -- there is no real Milton/London split to show for this specific driver subset." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#CCCCCC;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=15;spacingTop=12;spacingRight=15;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="137" width="1380" height="230" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

