        <mxCell id="panelB_note" value="&quot;HOS remaining at return&quot; is a single SNAPSHOT -- just the final leg of a whole multi-week cycle -- so it's close either way (REAL slightly higher, not a real story). It does NOT answer &quot;is the model maximizing legal hours without going over&quot; -- that needs every real work-day counted, not just the last one. See the Utilization panel below for that direct answer. Cycle duration: TRAINED does more trips and more revenue in 7% FEWER calendar hours per cycle -- genuinely tighter, less wasteful trip selection, not a rolling-window artifact (tested and confirmed directly)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5F9FF;strokeColor=#6C8EBF;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="835" width="1380" height="85" as="geometry" />
